      "role": "model_output",
      "slot": "s3",
      "source_id": "8c28f7bc-9596-4506-b79a-a2e791784cb2",
      "text": "Since you have different types of plants, it's really helpful to know exactly what they are to give specific advice! Generally, in very hot weather, it's best to check the soil's moisture level directly rather than just sticking to a schedule."
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "external",
      "slot": "s4",
      "source_id": "396b9298-6770-4e4c-9e9e-2e10d4cd6656",
      "text": "That's good to know. I'll go check the soil then. I was also wondering, do you think I should move any of them out of the direct sun? Some of the leaves are starting to look a little droopy."
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "model_output",
      "slot": "s5",
      "source_id": "5fd4c229-5607-444c-8f1b-75590bec0f73",
      "text": "Moving them out of the direct sun sounds like a very good idea right now, especially if they are starting to look droopy. If you're worried about the heat, putting them in a spot that gets filtered or dappled light should help significantly."
    }
